# Web (`apps/web`)

Read ADR-0003 (clients) and `docs/specs/44-web-ui-kit.md`.

- Routes under `src/app/[locale]/...`: thin async server components; the page container is
  `mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6`. Unknown data → `notFound()`.
- Features in `src/features/<feature>/` (`'use client'` components, hooks, api calls); primitives
  in `src/components/ui/` (shadcn new-york, cva variants, Radix); shell in `src/components/shell/`.
  New primitives get an entry in the dev showcase `/[locale]/dev/ui` (404 in production).
- Class names through `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts` (extends tailwind-merge with the token font
  sizes). Colors/spacing/radius/typography only from tokens (`bg-primary`, `p-md`, `text-title`…).
- **Tailwind gotcha:** named spacing tokens (`xs`…`5xl`) are 4–48px; `w-md`/`p-md` are spacing.
  `max-w-*`/`min-w-*` are pinned back to container sizes by the theme — keep it that way.
- Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (e.g. `text-primary` on `bg-secondary` fails — use `secondary-foreground`).
- Server-side API calls use `API_INTERNAL_URL` (fallback `PUBLIC_URL` + `/api/v1`), `cache:
  'no-store'` for user data, a timeout, and parse responses with the contract schema. Browser
  calls go to same-origin `/api/v1` (dev rewrite in `next.config.ts`, Caddy in production).
- Locale routing lives in `src/proxy.ts` (Next 16 middleware) and sets `x-next-intl-locale`; do not
  add two-letter top-level routes (they would be treated as locales).
- Forms: react-hook-form + the contract zod schema + `FormField`; map `VALIDATION_FAILED.details`
  to fields; buttons show a loading state and are disabled while submitting; success → toast.
- Every data view handles loading (skeleton), empty (with CTA) and error (message + retry); works
  on narrow and wide layouts and with the keyboard (UI-STD).
- Tests: Vitest + Testing Library (`vitest.setup.ts` registers `cleanup()`); wrap in
  `NextIntlClientProvider` and assert catalog texts; mock `next/navigation` and `fetch`.
- `@types/react` is pinned via `tsconfig.json` `paths` (mobile hoists another version) — keep it.
